/-! # Unit PH: `callerMix` — the first PARENT on the new boundary, at the level of the four check premises

`Sparkle.Tests.Compiler.ShippingPremiseEvalTest.callerMix` calls two DISTINCT one-output gate children
(`pick`, `pickD`) in the one-output closing.  Its old checks are `callerMix.machine_factsH`,
`machine_outsH`, `machine_hierTypedH`, `machine_designFullH` (generated by `#machine_oneout`; they take
`hB : ChildBnd`, `closes : MachineClosesAt`, the run, `MachineDefines`, one `EntryDefines` per callee).
Here the same four statements are proved from the ported chain
(`Tools.ShippingParentDesignA`, `Tools.ShippingParentPortsA`, `Tools.ShippingParentGateA`) with

    (O : RefLawsAOps MkRefd mref cref) (hA : AdmCtx O.quiet mctx cctx)
    (T : RefLawsATele O.quiet mref cref) (hw : JQ O.quiet 0 w)

in place of `hB`, and `MachineClosesAtA` DISCHARGED by `machineClosesAtA_of_gateKids` (RESTRICTED: the
callees are pairwise distinct, `hnodup`, decided here).  Every data condition is the generated
`callerMix.oneout_*`.

NOT claimed: the old endpoint `callerMix.machine_design_svH_full` is NOT ported (its semantic part
`machine_composedRA`/`ServedReal`/`soundL` still takes `ChildBnd`: OPEN).  These four statements are the
four check premises of `machine_design_svHR`, not the endpoint.  No runtime-fit claim; `O`, `hA`, `T`,
`hw` are hypotheses; `RealChildA` is a history. -/

